{"author":{"id":"f4f7e123ea38957901744390924e1710825e6d55b5113472173231f66fb2d926"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795285254,"nonce":"154rHoXysY1pk/mG4rPVk9fbylg=","message":"Completed in PR #25, https://github.com/evvaletov/gw-basic-2026/pull/25, merged as 343cf6647fa53cecede524c580efa4ba4a0dcfb2. Reviewed source 7bda436d37b6b2ad357b3a5dc4a129b7f20bb1b0 has the identical Git tree. All final-head PR CI checks passed. Review bundle: /mhd/150_GW_BASIC_2026_debugger_corpus_2026-11-21.\n\nThe scripted interpreter monitor is integrated into main on POSIX and DOS16/32. The POSIX two-terminal curses controller displays entry source, watches and native inspection events and supports step/continue, breaks, inspect/checkpoints, detach and cancellation. Program input and graphics retain their terminal. The shared FORTRAN line protocol is byte-identical.\n\nValidation includes 11 native monitor tests, 24 controller tests (21 controlling-PTY cases and three pipe-based paths), 16 ordinary terminal-input tests and actual DOS16/32 execution, screen and file-inspection checks. Seven independent QA/prose/elegance rounds ended with no blocking findings.\n\nThis issue stays open for next/finish, VS Code/DAP, completion and other frontends; AOT needs explicit instrumentation and source maps. Current source builds are required; v0.18.3 downloads predate this work. Optional later hardening: close debugger descriptors on exec, avoid repeated early-detach lock probes, move continued-run signal masking after the stop decision, and check CPU use after terminal loss during cancellation. SHELL descendants and a forcibly killed launcher are outside cancellation cleanup guarantees.","files":null}]}